target_id":"ec76-0603-ea06-4778"},{"link_uuid":"9c743ff8-c56d-4ccf-88df-5fc281bd4d32","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"454b-1740-8fbc-4950"},{"link_uuid":"97a7ba09-6637-4b50-9387-05986bf78d55","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"0a92-31b6-358d-43d2"},{"link_uuid":"2cb4260b-75f3-46aa-b6a0-ad1243c414a6","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"a83e-57bc-00bb-45e5"},{"link_uuid":"0af4aaf9-293b-4330-ae10-b8f81a46db7f","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"da57-123c-cfff-4e9b"},{"link_uuid":"7699979b-c16c-42a0-8c67-e31b48718512","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"12fb-d208-1fa5-4860"},{"link_uuid":"f74f68b6-8db3-49dd-bda7-5eda6ea31f67","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"ac68-e19c-88df-4db0"},{"link_uuid":"cd2b60f4-0bf2-464b-8b3d-f2e76b42de7d","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"a4b6-a02d-53bd-44cb"},{"link_uuid":"0978b4c9-d1ee-4834-a335-33a20ca32f71","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"15bb-0b78-43b8-4ab8"},{"link_uuid":"2e74146b-0be0-4d37-944a-576645d74958","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"9fdd-8c4e-4934-45f8"},{"link_uuid":"c744b42d-6ddf-4a0f-8518-2f7aced5feb4","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"c3fe-e28b-0213-4a94"},{"link_uuid":"ed9d4a3a-fdcf-400b-a251-b4192e9ac9a8","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"be18-a678-846d-4406"},{"link_uuid":"b811d5e3-de64-4920-a5e0-5afff9c18ae0","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"25c8-e7e4-9d53-4c4b"},{"link_uuid":"bc702e65-a41d-44d4-b352-9ac9deb038bd","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"8c97-d24a-1425-4980"},{"link_uuid":"f3fc76d2-5dcb-4fa6-9641-ac2a102ffbf0","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"08e8-ff5c-107e-463b"},{"link_uuid":"3dcddeec-0104-4d9e-ae12-f16c618a9bea","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"3b57-41d9-a401-42ce"},{"link_uuid":"f7e61766-6dfd-4f28-918c-f3e0525fff87","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"eec1-8a7c-4628-43c2"},{"link_uuid":"2294f136-0016-407b-b896-3019d2810775","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"3e68-115a-1160-4d11"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe tests/unit cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_push_policy.py:1-18` — Preserve universal no-`tickets`-push invariant and directory enumeration. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py:1-16, 874-909, 942-959, 996-1014, 1095-1105, 1314-1326` — Preserve pre/post-merge parity, timeout/crash policies, optionality coverage, and stale-tree behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_claim_default_assignee.py:109-118, 152-162` — Preserve relocated-store repo-root requirement for assignee and plan gate. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_cli_body_guard.py:1-22` — Preserve option-looking-body refusal, surplus rejection, and `--` escape. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_cli_json_js_safe_guard.py:1-10` — Preserve unsafe stdout discrimination, sanctioned marker, parse failure, and gate wiring. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_cli_registry_cutover_s6_heldout.py:1-16` — Preserve adversarial dispatch/single-authority/retired-route/identity contracts. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_cli_registry_cutover_s6.py:1-19` — Preserve handler metadata, adapter/init policy, and unified dispatch. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_cli_registry_dispatch.py:1-22` — Preserve selected-handler laziness, adapter shapes, init, one parse, and public behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_cli_registry_split.py:1-12` — Preserve re-export identity, complete check registration, and public validation teeth. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_cli_registry.py:1-13, 238-243, 245-249` — Preserve sole routing authority, derived policy sets, and lazy imports. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_close_autoresume_b5f8.py:1-17, 246-251` — Preserve insufficiency-only retry qualification, strict progress/bounds, and retryable exhausted result. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_close_disposition_attestation_738a.py:1-15, 37-46, 79-89, 117-125` — Preserve signed disposition, supported classes, force-withholds-signature, and close-path wiring. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_close_gate_bound_message_d59e.py:1-26, 95-102, 122-131` — Preserve cause-specific remedy, genuine-unavailability control, and non-size recovery distinction. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_close_gate_bound_remedy_db1c.py:1-38, 114-120, 133-138, 149-155, 166-172, 182-187` — Preserve attestation cost, append-only limitation, diagnosis, and actionable alternative. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_close_gate_disposition_69b9.py:1-22` — Preserve link-backed disposition exemption and distinct audit verdict. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_close_gate_step_budget_message_d59e.py:1-26` — Preserve step-budget-specific remediation and distinction from missing runtime. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_close_precheck_duplicate_link_c8fd.py:1-17, 110-115, 144-151, 236-241` — Preserve actionable link command, closed canonical acceptance, no-LLM behavior, and class scoping. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_close_precheck_message_fb8b.py:1-31` — Preserve file-impact diagnosis, re-attestation consequence, paths/SHA, and remedy. Consumer: none found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope rem